[Puzzle "The ...e4 fork"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "10...e4"]
[End "10...e4"]
[Hint "White's last move ignored the threat you made with 9...e5. What was it?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 e6 4. Nf3 Bd6 5. Bg3 O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 7. c3 Qc7 8. Bd3 Nbd7 9. O-O e5 10. Bh4?? e4! {[%cal Ge4f3,Ge4d3] Forks the knight on f3 and the bishop on d3, and White can't save both.}
(10... exd4? {Opens the center, but lets White off the hook.} 11. exd4 Re8 12. Re1 Rxe1+ 13. Qxe1 b6 14. Bg3 Bb7 {Stockfish: +0.2, equal.})
11. dxc5 {White's best try: it grabs a pawn.} Bxc5 12. Bc2 exf3 {You have won a piece for a pawn. Stockfish: −5.9, winning for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "Take the bishop first"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "8...exf4"]
[End "8...exf4"]
[Hint "Your knight on c6 is attacked. Is there something bigger to take first?"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Bf4 g6 3. e3 Bg7 4. Nf3 O-O 5. Bd3 d6 6. c3 Nc6 7. Nbd2 e5 8. d5?? exf4! {[%cal Ge5f4] Takes the bishop. If White takes the knight, you take on e3 and stay a piece up.}
(8... Nxd5! {Also good: takes the pawn, and the bishop on f4 is still attacked.} 9. Bg5 Nde7 10. e4 f6 11. Bh4 {Black has won a pawn. Stockfish: −2.2, winning for Black.})
(8... Ne7!? {Playable: the knight steps away, and Black wins the pawn on d5 next.} 9. Bg3 Nfxd5 10. e4 Nf6 11. O-O {Stockfish: −2.0, winning for Black.})
(8... Nb8? {Saves the knight, but now White's bishop escapes.} 9. Bg5 h6 10. Bxf6 Qxf6 11. O-O c6 12. c4 Qd8 {Stockfish: −0.5, slightly better for Black.})
9. dxc6 fxe3 10. fxe3 Qe8 {[%cal Ge8e3,Ge8c6] The queen hits e3 and c6, and White's king is stuck in the center. Stockfish: −4.7, winning for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "Break the pin"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "10...g5"]
[End "10...g5"]
[Hint "Your f6 knight is pinned to the queen. How can you chase the bishop away?"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Bf4 g6 3. e3 Bg7 4. Nf3 O-O 5. Bd3 d6 6. c3 Nc6 7. Nbd2 e5 8. Bg5 h6 9. Bh4 Qe7 10. O-O? g5! {[%cal Gg5h4] Hits the bishop and breaks the pin. Now ...e4 threatens to fork the knight on f3 and the bishop on d3.}
(10... e4? {Too early: the f6 knight is still pinned.} 11. Nxe4 g5 12. Nxf6+ Qxf6 13. Bg3 Ne7 {White has won a pawn, and your kingside is loose. Stockfish: +3.1, winning for White.})
11. Nxg5 {White's best: a knight for two pawns.}
(11. Bg3? e4! 12. Nxg5 exd3 {You have won a piece for a pawn. Stockfish: −4.6, winning for Black.})
11... hxg5 12. Bxg5 d5! {[%cal Gd5e4] Takes e4 away from White. You have a knight for two pawns. Stockfish: −1.5, clearly better for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "The Greek gift with Ne4"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Attack the king"]
[Solve "13.Bxh7+"]
[End "15.Ne4"]
[Hint "Black's knight has left f6. What is guarding h7 now?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nd2 e6 6. Ngf3 Bd6 7. Bg3 O-O 8. Bd3 Qe7 9. Ne5 Nd7 10. Nxd7 Bxd7 11. Bxd6 Qxd6 12. dxc5 Qxc5? 13. Bxh7+! {[%cal Gd3h7] The Greek gift: only the king guards h7.}
(13. O-O? {Natural, but the chance is gone.} Rfd8 14. Qh5 g6 15. Qg5 Kg7 16. Rfd1 {Stockfish: −0.1, equal.})
13... Kxh7 14. Qh5+ {[%hint Bring the queen to the kingside with check.] With check, so Black has no time for anything else.} Kg8
15. Ne4 {[%hint Which piece can hit the queen on c5 and head for g5 at the same time?] [%cal Ge4c5,Ge4g5] Hits the queen and threatens Ng5 with mate on h7. 15...dxe4 opens the fifth rank, and 16.Qxc5 wins the queen.}
15... g6 {The best defense: it stops mate, and the queens come off.} 16. Nxc5 gxh5 17. Nxd7 Rfc8 18. Nf6+ Kf8 19. Nxh5 {You are two pawns up, and Black's kingside is wrecked. Stockfish: +3.1, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The Greek gift with Qh4"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Attack the king"]
[Solve "14.Bxh7+"]
[End "16.Ng5"]
[Hint "Black's queen has just left d8. Which square did it guard there?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nd2 e6 6. Ngf3 Bd6 7. Bg3 O-O 8. Bd3 b6 9. e4 dxe4 10. Nxe4 Nxe4 11. Bxe4 Bb7 12. dxc5 Bxc5 13. Qa4 Qc8?? 14. Bxh7+! {[%cal Ge4h7] The bishop leaves e4, and the fourth rank opens for your queen.}
(14. O-O? {Natural, but Black gets time to cover h4 again.} h6 15. Rad1 a5 16. Bc2 Ne7 17. Ne5 {Stockfish: +0.3, slightly better for White.})
14... Kxh7 15. Qh4+ {[%hint Your queen can reach the kingside along the fourth rank.] With check.} Kg8
16. Ng5 {[%hint Which knight move threatens mate on h7?] [%cal Gh4h7] Threatens Qh7#.}
16... Rd8 17. Qh7+ Kf8 18. Qh8+ Ke7 19. Qxg7 {[%cal Gg7f7] You have two pawns for the bishop, Black's king is stuck in the center, and more material will fall. Stockfish: +6.4, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Save the rook"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Keep the extra piece"]
[Solve "9.Qb1"]
[End "9.Qb1"]
[Hint "Black's queen attacks your rook on a1. Your knight has already left b1."]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nd2 Qb6 6. Qb3 c4 7. Qc2 Bf5?? 8. Qxf5 Qxb2 9. Qb1! {[%cal Gb1b2] Guards the rook and offers a queen trade. You keep the extra piece.}
(9. Rd1!? {Playable: it saves the rook too, but after 9...Qxc3 the knight on d2 is pinned and Black's queen stays active.} 9... Qxc3 10. Qb1 Qb4 11. Be2 e6 12. Nf3 {Stockfish: +0.9, slightly better for White. 9.Qb1 keeps a bigger edge.})
(9. Rb1? {Saves the rook, but after 9...Qxc3 the knight on d2 is pinned, and Black's pawns and active queen make up for the piece.} Qxc3 10. Ne2 Qa5 11. Qc2 e6 12. Nc3 Bb4 {Stockfish: 0.0, equal.})
9... Qxc3 10. Nf3 Qb4 11. Be2 {You have a piece for two pawns, and Black's queen will be chased. Stockfish: +3.2, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The poisoned b-pawn"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "5.Nxd5"]
[End "5.Nxd5"]
[Hint "Nothing guards d5 now. What would a knight on c7 attack?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 c5 3. e3 Qb6 4. Nc3 Qxb2?? 5. Nxd5! {[%cal Gd5c7,Ga1b1] Threatens Nc7+, forking king and rook, and Rb1 to trap the queen.}
(5. Bb5+! {Also good.} Kd8 6. Nge2 {Black's king can no longer castle. Stockfish: +2.9, winning for White.})
(5. Rb1?? {Chases the queen, but it takes the knight with check.} Qxc3+ 6. Qd2 Qxd2+ 7. Kxd2 Nf6 {Black is a piece up. Stockfish: −6.9, winning for Black.})
5... Nf6 6. Rb1 Qxa2 7. Nc7+ Kd8 8. Nxa8 {You have won a rook. Stockfish: +7.0, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The knight blocks the queen"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "9...Bxd3"]
[End "9...Bxd3"]
[Hint "Is White's bishop on d3 really protected?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 c5 3. e3 cxd4 4. exd4 Nc6 5. c3 Bf5 6. Nf3 e6 7. Nbd2 Bd6 8. Bxd6 Qxd6 9. Bd3?? Bxd3! {[%cal Gf5d3] [%csl Rd2] The knight on d2 cuts White's queen off from d3, so the bishop can't be taken back.}
(9... Nxd4? {Grabs a pawn, but misses the piece.} 10. Qa4+ Nc6 11. Bxf5 exf5 12. O-O {Stockfish: −0.2, equal.})
10. Nb3 Bf5 11. Nh4 Nh6 12. O-O Qe7 13. Nxf5 Nxf5 {You have won a piece. Stockfish: −6.3, winning for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "Trap the bishop"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "3...e5"]
[End "3...e5"]
[Hint "White's bishop on f4 has few squares left. Which pawn move attacks it?"]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 h5 3. e3?? e5! {[%cal Ge5f4] Hits the bishop. Next ...g5 and ...h4 trap it.}
(3... Bf5? {Natural, but it lets White off the hook.} 4. Bd3 Bxd3 5. Qxd3 e6 {Stockfish: +0.4, slightly better for White.})
4. Bxe5 {White's best: give up the bishop for pawns at once.}
(4. dxe5? g5! 5. Bg3 h4 {The bishop is trapped. Stockfish: −4.7, winning for Black.})
4... f6 5. Bf4 g5 6. Be2 gxf4 7. Bxh5+ Kd7 8. Bg4+ Ke8 {You have won the bishop for two pawns. Stockfish: −1.7, clearly better for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "The Englund trap"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Escape the trap"]
[Solve "6.Nc3"]
[End "6.Nc3"]
[Hint "Black's queen hits your rook on a1, and Bc3 walks into a trap. Look for a developing move that frees your first rank."]

1. d4 e5 2. dxe5 Nc6 3. Nf3 Qe7 4. Bf4 Qb4+ 5. Bd2 Qxb2 6. Nc3! {[%cal Gd1a1] Develops, guards a2, and clears b1, so your queen now guards a1. Rb1 comes next.}
(6. Bc3?? {Hits the queen, but walks into a mate.} Bb4! 7. Qd2 Bxc3 8. Qxc3 Qc1#)
6... Bb4 7. Rb1 Qa3 8. Nd5 {[%cal Gd5c7] Threatens Nxc7+, forking the king and rook.} Bxd2+ 9. Qxd2 Kd8 10. e4 {Material is level, but you are far ahead in development, and Black's king can no longer castle. Stockfish: +3.4, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Take the bishop, then hit the queen"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "12.Nxg4"]
[End "13.dxc5"]
[Hint "Black's bishop on g4 has only the knight to guard it. Take it, then look for a move that hits Black's queen."]

1. d4 d5 2. Bf4 Nf6 3. e3 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Nbd2 e6 7. Bb5 Bd6 8. Qa4 O-O 9. Bxc6 bxc6 10. Bxd6 Qxd6 11. Ne5 Rfc8? 12. Nxg4! {[%cal Ge5g4] Takes the bishop. The knight that takes back will be left without a guard.}
(12. Nb3? {Guards d4, but the bishop on g4 gets away.} 12... cxd4 13. cxd4 Bh5 {Stockfish: +1.0, clearly better for White.})
12... Nxg4 13. dxc5! {[%hint Black's queen is on d6, and the knight on g4 has no guard.] [%cal Gc5d6,Ga4g4] Hits the queen. When it moves, your queen takes the knight on g4.} Qe7 14. Qxg4 {You have won a piece. Stockfish: +4.3, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The fork on c7"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "6.Nb5"]
[End "6.Nb5"]
[Hint "The c7 square is empty, and Black's king and rook stand on e8 and a8. Which knight can reach c7?"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 Nc6 5. Nc3 d5? 6. Nb5! {[%cal Gb5c7,Gf4c7] Threatens Nc7+, forking the king and the rook on a8. The bishop on f4 hits c7 too.}
(6. Be2? {Develops, but Black gets time to cover c7.} 6... a6 {Stockfish: 0.0, equal.})
6... Kd7 {Black's best, but the king is stuck in the middle.} 7. Ng5 {[%cal Gg5f7] The other knight joins in, aiming at f7. Stockfish: +2.0, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "Ng5 and the fork on f7"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Punish the mistake"]
[Solve "8.Ng5"]
[End "8.Ng5"]
[Hint "Black's ...a6 stopped Bb5+. Only the king guards f7, and your knight on e5 already hits it. What can join in?"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 b6 5. Nbd2 Bb7 6. Nc4 d5 7. Nce5 a6? 8. Ng5! {[%cal Gg5f7,Ge5f7] Both knights hit f7, and only the king guards it. A knight on f7 would fork queen and rook.}
(8. Bd3? {Develops, but the chance is gone.} 8... Nc6 9. c3 Bd6 {Stockfish: +0.5, slightly better for White.})
8... Rg8 {Black's best try: the rook steps out of the fork.}
(8... cxd4 9. exd4 Ne4 10. Ngxf7 {[%cal Gf7d8,Gf7h8] The fork: queen and rook are both hit. Stockfish: +3.2, winning for White.})
9. Nexf7 Qd7 10. Ne5 {[%cal Ge5d7] White is a pawn up and hits the queen again. Black's rook has left h8, so Black can't castle kingside. Stockfish: +2.9, winning for White.}
*
